Z||000000||rigdonhome||09-08-2001||01:04 PM||||As if that weren't enough to talk my way out of, I was in an '88 GT still owned by the guy I bought it from in Connecticut, and I had Michigan plates on it from another car!  <P>After lots of begging and pleading, I ended up with just the speeding ticket...  ($204)<P>His advice was:  "I would suggest that you take the time to straighten out your registration, and until then try not to do anything to draw attention to yourself, like driving 100mph!!!"<P>He makes a good point.<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_driving_signature.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/rear_signature.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_rear_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000001||hugh||09-08-2001||04:08 PM||||You're lucky you didn't get ticketed for being too young!Who worked the pedals?||||reg||1
Z||000002||RedRavenGT||09-08-2001||06:33 PM||||Something similar happened to me. Except my speeding was only 41 in a 25.<P>I had just finished putting a different engine in my 86 GT that I got from the Fiero Warehouse (Thanks Doug!!). I decided to put my plates from my 85 SE on it so I could test drive it a couple of days. Well I got stopped. Heres what the prick cop gave me:<P>Speeding: $16<BR>Proof of Liability: $150<BR>Ficticious Registation: $150<BR>Court Fees: $25<P>Now on top of this, its been 2 months now since it happened, I got a letter yesterday in the mail saying that on the 26th of this month I will be suspended indefinately.<P>Apperantly ND has passed a new law with proof of liability. I have to surrender my old license. Buy a new one for $50 with a restriction on it requiring proof of insurance (meaning if I get stopped the cop has to ask for proof)for 3 yrs. My insurance company has to inform the DOT if I drop my policy.<P>Then after 3 yrs I have to purchase another license for $50 to get the restriction off of it!!!<P>I think criminals have more rights then a normal citizen. If you dont read them their rights, they walk, no matter how guilty they are!!!!!!!!!  ASSHOLESSS!!!!!!!!!<P><BR>But hey, Im not bitter..<P>Oh yea. Forgot to mention that I got 9 points taken off my license too..<P>Sorry so long...<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Jul02$03.jpg">  <BR>(formerly known as V8Fiero)<p>[This message has been edited by RedRavenGT (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||prtzlboy||09-08-2001||09:24 PM||||*ouch*<P>Holy smokes that's HARSH.  We sure live in a messed up world hehe.||||reg||1
Z||000004||artherd||09-09-2001||04:17 AM||||I have been ticketed for drag-racing against myself...  twice...<P>And for 'impersonating' a police officer (I was in costume on the way to a buddy's short fil, guess what I was playing?)<P>Oh, and my father's car was stolen from his driveway Memorial day weekend, guess what the cops did? <P>Yeah, that much.<P>Grrrr! that was my weekely police ***** , stay tuned for next week!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000005||rigdonhome||09-09-2001||09:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>You're lucky you didn't get ticketed for being too young!Who worked the pedals?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Is that a short joke???<P>Actually, that is my 12-month old Son, Ezra.  He is a gearhead already and loves for me to let him steer!  The only toys he will play with are those with wheels, and he naps with his favorite Hot Wheels!<P>Cheers,<BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_driving_signature.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/rear_signature.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/ezra_rear_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||12
Z||000006||Boomtastic||09-09-2001||10:09 AM||||How about this one? I was sent a ticket, by mail, for 80 in a 25 zone, which totalled $400. The ticket had to be mailed because I OUTRAN the officer in her police cruiser! At 2 in the morning, I'm headed for home, and she's a quarter mile plus behind me without her lights on. I take a turn and she looses me, and THAT'S outrunning her? Anyways, she called in that she was chasing a yellow Fiero and lost it. 20 minutes later and 2 towns away, 2 local police are shooting the breeze on the town line, and here I come putting along at the speed limit. (Radar detectors do work at times.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) They pulled me over and asked a few questions ("Where are you coming from?" "Where are ya headed?" etc.) and left me with a 'bogus' speeding ticket. I use that term 'bogus' because the officer, upon handing it to me, immediately proceeded to tell me how to fight it. He had no intention of pursuing the ticket if I contested it, and told me flat out. It seemed weird, but I took it as a "Hey, we got the bad guy for ya" type of traffic stop. Withing minutes I was on my way, but the damage was already done. All of my information - license, reg, etc. was broadcast over the police channel, and guess who was listening? Yep - the cop that I outran. She mailed me a ticket, which btw is against the law (the officer needs to prove that it was me driving .. it could have been someone else, and she couldn't prove otherwise. I never admitted I was there. Keep in mind your 5th Ammendment rights at all times!), and I immediately fought it. I lost the first preliminary hearing because the officer lied about the route, and the Magistrate didn't believe anything I said. I even brought notarized docs to support my story, however they were not allowed in as evidence (the Magistrate refused to even look at them). I appealed, and the case was thrown out. In the end, I ended up paying $150 for the lawyer, and lost 2 days pay, which added up to approx. $400.<P>Ain't America great?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
